{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-007",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 7,
  "title": "Job 7",
  "display_title": "Job 7",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 7,
  "sortOrder": 18007,
  "verseCount": 21,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Is there not an appointed time to man upon earth? are not his days also like the days of an hireling?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "As a servant earnestly desireth the shadow, and as an hireling looketh for the reward of his work:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "So am I made to possess months of vanity, and wearisome nights are appointed to me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "When I lie down, I say, When shall I arise, and the night be gone? and I am full of tossings to and fro unto the dawning of the day.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "My flesh is clothed with worms and clods of dust; my skin is broken, and become loathsome.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle, and are spent without hope.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "O remember that my life is wind: mine eye shall no more see good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The eye of him that hath seen me shall see me no more: thine eyes are upon me, and I am not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "As the cloud is consumed and vanisheth away: so he that goeth down to the grave shall come up no more.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "He shall return no more to his house, neither shall his place know him any more.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Therefore I will not refrain my mouth; I will speak in the anguish of my spirit; I will complain in the bitterness of my soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Am I a sea, or a whale, that thou settest a watch over me?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "When I say, My bed shall comfort me, my couch shall ease my complaint;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Then thou scarest me with dreams, and terrifiest me through visions:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "So that my soul chooseth strangling, and death rather than my life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "I loathe it; I would not live alway: let me alone; for my days are vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "What is man, that thou shouldest magnify him? and that thou shouldest set thine heart upon him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And that thou shouldest visit him every morning, and try him every moment?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "How long wilt thou not depart from me, nor let me alone till I swallow down my spittle?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "I have sinned; what shall I do unto thee, O thou preserver of men? why hast thou set me as a mark against thee, so that I am a burden to myself?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:7:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "And why dost thou not pardon my transgression, and take away mine iniquity? for now shall I sleep in the dust; and thou shalt seek me in the morning, but I shall not be.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 7:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:7:21"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "repository": "aruljohn/Bible-kjv",
